## E3 census — derived nodes and their version anchor
e3 rule: a derived node (Point/Object/Event) carries a version anchor iff it is the SOURCE of at least one extractedFrom relationship whose sourceVersion is a non-empty string, OR the TARGET of at least one references relationship whose sourceVersion is a non-empty string. The two directions are NOT interchangeable: extractedFrom points FROM the derived node at its source ((Point)-[:extractedFrom]->(GraphEvent|Event)), while references points AT the derived node ((Source)-[:references]->(Event|Document) — tortoise/projection/edges.py:2432-2457 link_source_to_event, reached from the capture path at tortoise/sdk.py:14398 (proj.link_source_to_event(source_key, event_id))). The anchor is a property of the DERIVATION LINK (tortoise/projection/edges.py:502-510 _anchor_on_create/_DERIVATION_ANCHOR_SET), and the references target labels are _DERIVATION_REFERENCES_LABELS (edges.py:475: Event, Document). A Source->Object link is identity/mention and carries none BY DESIGN (owner option A, #5199; #9736)
