## why each non-green row is not green
row E1 note: the only E1 artifact is docs/evidence/7949-capstone/e1-e2.log: before=0.600000 after=0.600000 objects=25 bound=0.300000 vs bar after_share <= 0.5 x before_share (Objects floor 30) — after_share is NOT <= 0.5 x before_share, so the arithmetic would FAIL — but the row is NOT RED, because the record's own floor makes it REFUSED: the artifact's denominator is 25 Objects (under the frozen floor of 30) and is the 25-name owner-labelled audit population rather than 'all :Object nodes written by the run'. Its corpus (e78d306ccb4bce73459c5c22b61122140ba860b1108d3eba2ebecb661cbdfe6b) is not the frozen corpus (sha256:dd7e85200f4809f701b9e9c11816b541acea63afd0b2472998975e2ebcb035dc), and the artifact declares prereg=UNPREREGISTERED result=UNPREREGISTERED. No before/after pair on the pre-registered corpus exists, and the mechanism that must move the share is an owner ruling on removal/relocation (#5333) — so no scored E1 measurement exists to be red
row E2 note: E2a: BLOCKED — values=42 (the frozen 14-unit denominator is not carried by any committed artifact) vs bar 13 of 14. E2b: PASS — fused=1/114 = 0.008772 vs bar fused share <= 0.05 (floor 30 surviving units) (a proxy: the artifact counts atomic POINTS, not surviving planted units). The E2 row is BLOCKED because the composite criterion needs BOTH halves and E2a's frozen 14-value-bearing-unit denominator is carried by no committed artifact; the artifact's no-loss control (values 42 before and after, real_facts 90) is consistent with E2a but does not compute it. Same corpus caveat as E1: e78d306ccb4bce73459c5c22b61122140ba860b1108d3eba2ebecb661cbdfe6b is not sha256:dd7e85200f4809f701b9e9c11816b541acea63afd0b2472998975e2ebcb035dc, and #9775 records that the state-value carve-out is absent on one render path
row E3 note: anchored=163 derived=458 share=0.355895; bar share = 1.0 (zero unanchored), floor 30 derived nodes; measured on THIS run's own graph (capstone_on_54922a800_1793378318, fixtures_hash sha256:dd7e85200f4809f701b9e9c11816b541acea63afd0b2472998975e2ebcb035dc). The Source->Object identity link carries no sourceVersion BY DESIGN (owner option A, #5199), so ':Object mention links' can never anchor — and the frozen denominator counts them anyway, so the = 1.000 bar is unreachable as registered (#9736: either the metric is re-registered or the model is reopened; a lane cannot pick). COMPOSITION of the 353 Point nodes the denominator also counts: 159 mechanical turn rows + 156 extraction claims (156 anchored) + 29 operator Points (0 anchored) + 9 other (0 anchored), each class read off the property its writer stamps. TWO of those classes cannot carry a derivation link AT ALL and are named rather than folded into the figure: the turn rows carry none BY CONSTRUCTION (_TURN_WRITE_CYPHER in _write_capture_turns, tortoise/sdk.py:2377, t.is_episodic=true, wired only by CONTAINS), and the operator Points are written by create_operator (tortoise/sdk.py — the IMPL/NAND/INPUT operator writer), which never writes extractedFrom. So counting them under 'all derived nodes' is defensible but they can never anchor and are not a provenance shortfall, and a denominator summing them would report a shortfall nothing could close. The DERIVATION figure is anchored / expected-to-derive over the WRITER class (non-episodic, non-operator Points = the extraction claims PLUS the 'other' Points, which are the class where a LOST derivation link lands — Points with no extractedFrom that are neither turn rows nor operator Points): 156/165 = 0.945455. It is computed over that class and NOT over the claims alone, because a denominator defined by the extractedFrom link itself cannot move when that link is lost: the earlier reading divided by the extraction claims ALONE — the class that link defines — so it read nothing but 1.000000 BY CONSTRUCTION, with the 'other' Points sitting outside it. Whether an unanchored 'other' Point lost a link or was minted by a writer that never derives is the attribution #9736 still owns. #9736 must choose between re-registering the metric and reopening the model, and this row reports BOTH readings so neither choice is made on a denominator whose composition was hidden
row E4 note: edge_correct=2 planted=15; bar 15 of 15; content_ok=8 operators_total=27 on the SAME receipt. Its own date=2026-10-19T01:39:26Z, commit=6164c683c and corpus_hash=sha256:943a99ec619b4c67b8e31fefb90316ea023bbaddd1905d835b9d930243518324 differ from the frozen corpus (sha256:dd7e85200f4809f701b9e9c11816b541acea63afd0b2472998975e2ebcb035dc), and its verdict=regression failure_origin=gate_regression: the planted edges are not formed at all (#8503), and the receipt's retrievability rate is UNMEASURED (#9596)
row E5 note: ratio=1.0833 raw=0.4800 narrative=0.5200 n=25; bar ratio >= 0.9 AND raw >= 0.8 (floor 10 sentences); raw recovery = 1 - 0.52 = 0.4800 FAILS the 0.80 absolute floor while the 1.0833 ratio passes 0.90 — the record's own note says the ratio alone is degenerate, which is why the absolute floor exists. The re-score grades the 2026-10-18 arm receipts against THIS commit's gold (the gold is part of fixtures_hash) and warns INCOMPLETE RECEIPTS: wp07_bluepeak_followup:raw partial=True truncated=False s2_error=None s1_error=False s1_truncated=False — its holdout delta cannot be certified. #9738 also records that §10's prior measurement was visible when the record claimed it was not, and that the 25-bound vs 29-marker populations must be reconciled before either number is called final

